This product includes software developed as part of the Arix project.

The Arix wake module is original work, independently rewritten from scratch, and
is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see the LICENSE file in this directory).
The current sources carry no third-party GPL/LGPL code.

An earlier iteration of this module did contain four files derived from Operit
(LGPL-3.0-or-later). Those files were deleted outright, and the module was rebuilt
around a different architecture -- a VAD/MFCC front end feeding a switchable
decision stage (fixed-phrase KWS, or embedding-prototype matching for user-recorded
phrases), rather than the original MFCC+DTW listener.

This is an independent rewrite, referencing others' ideas rather than carrying
their code.

